  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the probabilities of obtaining a favorable outcome and prefers the lottery with the higher probability of such an outcome. The relevant probabilities in the decision problem are: \n- For Lottery A: 33% chance of 2500 Euros (favorable), 66% chance of 2400 Euros (also favorable), and 1% chance of 0 Euros (unfavorable). Thus, the total probability of a favorable outcome (i.e., receiving at least 2400 Euros) is 33% + 66% = 99%. \n- For Lottery B: 100% chance of 2400 Euros, so the probability of a favorable outcome is 100%. \nTherefore, the reason can be applied: Lottery B has a higher probability (100%) of a favorable outcome compared to Lottery A (99%). The reason would thus prefer Lottery B.",
